WarnBridge is newly written experimental software in a user-approved public repository.
A public repository does not by itself select an open-source license.
No historical PBS implementation code was copied. Historical sources include
PBS All Rights Reserved notices; no reuse permission was established.

Runtime dependencies retain their upstream licenses (see uv.lock and installed
package metadata). SiliconDust source (LGPL-2.1) was consulted for interface
semantics only; hdhomerun_config is an external, separately installed tool.
Synthetic fixtures are identified in tests/fixtures/README.md. Golden byte/text
vectors were supplied by the user. No original private capture is distributed.
